    Add a multithreaded Geant4 mode to o2-sim
    
    This adds the --isMT mode, in which one sim process runs Geant4 with one transport thread per sim worker.
    
    - Each Geant4 worker thread asks the primary server for its sub-events and sends its hits to the merger, as a worker process does.
    - The VMC application is cloned per thread, with its own stack, random generator, external decayer and data channel.
    - The threads share one request channel to the primary server.
    - Their data channels are closed before the process exits, so that the merger receives all queued hits.
    - A worker leaves its event loop once the server has no more work, after an empty event.
    - Detector clones get their own hit buffers, and the worker volume map points at the worker's own modules.
    - The media energy cuts and the worker-only Geant4 commands are applied on the worker threads.
    - The cached magnetic field values are invalidated at the start of each track.
    - ShmManager takes a mutex for its allocations, and the single sim process occupies the whole shared region.
    - 16 detectors are enabled for MT; EMCAL, HMPID, ZDC, FOCAL, FT0 and FV0 needed fixes to their copy constructor or destructor.
    - --isMT stops with an error for other engines, for Geant4 built without multithreading, for VecGeom navigation, and for detectors not yet enabled for it.
    
    https://its.cern.ch/jira/browse/O2-7305
    https://github.com/vmc-project/geant4_vmc/pull/92
    
