    Move FairRoot simulation infrastructure into O2
    
    This is a step in the long-term refactoring towards a native Geant4
    simulation. It decouples O2 from FairRoot by moving the simulation
    infrastructure that o2-sim depends on into the O2 repository.
    
    The imported classes retain their existing interfaces, so no changes are
    required in the current simulation code. The runtime parameter database,
    analysis framework, and other components that are unused by O2 are not
    imported, as their functionality is already provided by CCDB and
    ConfigurableParam.
    
    Owning these classes locally will allow future refactoring and cleanup
    without changing the current simulation behaviour.
    
    The imported sources keep their upstream formatting and licence headers,
    so they live under a 3rdparty directory and are excluded from
    clang-format.
    
    Requires the corresponding alidist update (fairroot.sh removal from o2.sh)
    to avoid duplicate ROOT dictionaries.
    
