    Integration of monopoles in O2 framework (#15602)
    
    This commit adds the transport and detector response of magnetic monopoles to
    o2-sim when running with Geant4. Related to https://its.cern.ch/jira/browse/O2-6780
    
    Until now, a monopole could neither be defined as a particle nor lose energy in
    the detectors, since it has no electric charge and the standard Geant4 physics
    does not ionise for it.
    
      - Four new particles, `Monopole_symm`/`Monopole_asymm` and their antiparticles
        (PDG codes ±4110000 and ±4120000), are registered in `O2DatabasePDG` and
        the Geant4 particle table. The helpers are in `MonopoleParticles.h`.
      - `O2MonopolePhysics` provides the monopole ionisation (`mplIoni`) and a
        dedicated transport process with the full dual Lorentz force. It does not
        replace the global chord finder or the stepper requested by the VMC macro.
      - ITS and TPC `ProcessHits` let neutral monopoles deposit energy. ITS gets a
        monopole response and a data format, TPC uses a Bethe-Bloch based ionisation.
      - `GeneratorFactory` takes the monopole mass so that generator and transport
        agree, and the monopole hook is combined with the fast-sim hook.
    
      Everything is steered by three new `G4Params` options:
    
      - `G4.monopole` (default `false`) switches the monopole physics on.
      - `G4.monopoleMagneticCharge` is the charge in units of the Dirac charge (default 1).
      - `G4.monopoleMass` is the mass in GeV (default 100) and has to agree with the
        mass in `TDatabasePDG`, otherwise the run is fatal.
    
      A non-positive magnetic charge or mass, or monopole physics requested but not
      installed, are also fatal.
    
      By default nothing changes for the user: the particles are only defined and the
      lookups in ITS and TPC are only done when `G4.monopole` is set.
    
      The changes were validated with Schwinger pair-produced monopoles and several
      values of the magnetic charge.

