    TPC: fix the weight and grid scaling of the spline derivatives in addCorrections (#15994)
    
    * TPC: fix the weight scaling of the mixed spline derivative in addCorrections
    
    TPCFastSpaceChargeCorrectionHelper::addCorrections scaled the 4th parameter of each spline knot (the mixed derivative d2S/dudv)
    with the square of the weight: secMainScale * secMainScale for the main correction, ls * ls * ... for the added ones (ls is the
    weight times the z fade-out factor, 1 at the knots). A spline is linear in its parameters, so scaling the correction by w scales all
    of them by w.
    
    The correction was therefore right at the knots but wrong between them whenever a weight != 1 was used, e.g. the derivative map
    added with weight lumiScale in TPCScalerSpec::buildMap. The error is proportional to w - w^2. Measured with a production map and
    the derivative map of run 568041 (random points, vs the weighted point-by-point sum of getCorrectionLocal and of the inverse
