    Skip combined device creation for empty spec list in DigitizerWorkflow
    
      With --combine-devices, specCombiner() is called unconditionally for
      digitizerSpecs and for writerSpecs, but when a collection is empty the result
      is a combined device with no sub-tasks: DPL sees a device with no inputs,
      injects a Lifetime::Enumeration input (WorkflowHelpers.cxx) and can elect
      it as the CCDB/DISTSUBTIMEFRAME source.
    
      No digits are produced, and since the enumeration is unbounded there is no
      EOS either, meaning that the workflow hangs forever instead of failing.
    
      This is reached with --onlyDet FT0,CTP, where the FT0 digitizer and the CTP
      digitizer are pushed to specs directly and only the FT0 digit writer goes
      to writerSpecs, leaving digitizerSpecs empty. In anchored MC that is the
      detector group of any run taken without both FV0 and EMCAL, such as run
      537401, where the problem was found.

