    GPUTracking: replace the merger's goto with helper lambdas
    
    MSL supports neither goto nor labels. The label sat at the end of the loop body,
    so each jump was a continue for the outer loop that could not be written as one
    because it was issued from an inner loop.
    
    Two lambdas take over the chain walks that did the jumping: one advances a track
    along its segment chain and reports whether the target was met on the way, the
    other reports whether the target sits on either neighbour chain. Each jump then
    becomes a plain continue at the top level of the loop body. A null target lets
    the first one also cover the four walks that never tested for one, leaving the
    file three lines shorter than it is with the goto.
    
    Checked against the goto version by transcribing both loop bodies into a harness
    and comparing the skip decision and the resulting segment and neighbour links of
    every track over 400000 random link graphs, 71% of which took a skip path and
    100000 of which reached the merging stage: no differences.

