    GPU: let the constant-address-space constants be built on Metal
    
    A constructor's implicit `this` is generic in MSL 4.1, and a generic pointer does
    not reach the constant address space, so a class-type constant at program scope
    could not be constructed at all: gpustd::bitset for the DetID and GlobalTrackID
    masks, CfChargePos for INVALID_CHARGE_POS.
    
    MSL lets a member function be qualified with the address space of its `this`, so
    each of the two constructors gains a constant-qualified overload next to the
    existing one; for bitset that sits next to the __constant copy constructor
    OpenCL already needs for the same reason.
    
    Reading those constants back needs nothing further, with one exception:
    sTrackSources is derived with operator| from the constant sMasks and then
    indexed by isTrackSource. Rather than give bitset constant-qualified accessors
    as well, that pair is left out of device code on Metal exactly as it already is
    on OpenCL; its only caller is on the host.

