    alignment, so the operand is cast at the one point where the operation is
    issued. That cast has to be made in the address space the pointer is really in,
    since casting a threadgroup pointer to a device atomic is a hard error, hence
    the two overloads: threadgroup stays threadgroup for the *Shared entry points,
    anything else resolves to device.

