    * MatchCosmics: selection of cosmics in collision data, named presets
    
    In collision data nearly all seeds are collision tracks and TPC-only legs had their z ignored, so any two tracks back-to-back in
    the transverse plane were paired (PbPb: minutes per TF, tens of thousands of fake pairs). New settings, all off by default and
    switched on together by the preset physics-v1 (o2-cosmics-match-workflow --cosmics-preset physics-v1; --configKeyValues can still
    override single keys, unknown names are fatal):
    
    - Seed cuts: minSeedNClTPC, minSeedDCAxy and minSeedDCAxyNSigma reject short TPC fragments and seeds passing the beam line
      (cosmics through the beam line are indistinguishable from collision tracks anyway).
    - z test of TPC-only legs (constrainTPCOnlyZ): a one-side TPC-only track has z relative to its time0, z(t) = z + side*vD*(t-time0);
      a CE-crossing or non-TPC-only track has an absolute z. The legs are compared at a common time (same side, or one leg with known
      time); for legs on opposite sides z continuity fixes the common time, which must lie in both time brackets. That time, with its
      error sigma_z / (2 vD) (~0.3 mus), is used for the refit and as the time of the cosmic (before: the centre of the bracket overlap,
      tens of mus, which put the legs at the wrong z: cosmics run 562658 A x C chi2Match median 3.5e4 -> 43). For all other pairs the
      time error of the cosmic stays the half-width of the bracket overlap.
    - Same-half veto (vetoSameHalf): pairs whose two legs lie on the same side of the closest approach in the transverse plane (two
      pieces of one leg) are rejected; skipped when a leg's reference point is within 20 cm of the closest approach.
    - maxChi2Match: cut on the chi2 of the refitted top/bottom legs.
    - minPtOppositeSides: for TPC-only legs on opposite sides z continuity defines the time, so z does not reject random pairs (94 % of
      the PbPb candidates). Both legs (in checkPair, before the winner selection) and the refitted cosmic need pT above it (scaled with
      the field).
    
    Unconditionally, the seeds and the refit use the muon mass (and charge 1) for the material corrections instead of the TPC track's
    PID from dE/dx (a leg tagged as kaon or proton got that mass): cosmic MC 6987 -> 7003 correct pairs (0 wrong), cosmics run 562658
    357 -> 358; the refitted q/pt changes by +-0.4 % (MC) and +-1 % (562658) (q16-q84, pT < 20 GeV).
    
    physics-v1: pT > 1 GeV, |DCA_xy| > 3 cm and > 10 sigma, >= 30 TPC clusters; systematic errors for the leg comparison y 0.5 cm,
    snp 0.02, q/pt 0.05 (true pairs had pulls 2-4x too wide) with crude chi2 < 50; open per-parameter windows except tgl (3 sigma);
    chi2Match < 1000; z test and same-half veto on; minPtOppositeSides 2 GeV.
    Validation, TPC-only legs: cosmic MC with PbPb-like distortions 7003 of 8638 cosmics correct (81.1 %, 0 wrong pairs); cosmics run
    562658 358 cosmics; PbPb 2025 LHC25an 567939 (19 kHz) 0.37 cosmics per TF (3.90 without the pT cut), 568041 reconstructed from
    CTF 0.30 per TF (3203 in 10546 TFs; the PbPb numbers before the muon mass, which leaves 4 PbPb TFs unchanged).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * MatchCosmics: energy-loss sign along the muon's flight; optional energy-loss sign in the TPC refit
    
    The propagator applies the energy-loss correction along the direction of the track parameters (loss forward, gain backward), and
    refitWinners fits a cosmic from the bottom leg to the top one: after the inward refit of the bottom leg its parameters are inverted
    and carried up through the top leg, i.e. they describe a particle moving upward. A cosmic muon flies downward, from the top leg to
    the bottom leg, so only the inward refit of the bottom leg (backward along its parameters = backward along the flight) had the
    physical sign; the propagation of the inverted bottom leg to the top leg, the outward refit of the top leg, the inward refit of the
    top leg, its propagation to the bottom parameter and the propagation of the top seeds to the DCA had the opposite one. The sign is
    now imposed along the flight in all of them, with the propagator's signCorr argument.
    
    GPUO2InterfaceRefit / GPUTrackingRefit::RefitTrackAsTrackParCov (TrackParCov + cluster references) get the analogous optional last
    argument eLossSign, passed to their propagations (0 = along the parameters as before, +1 gain, -1 loss; flipped on the optional
    way to the reference X when that runs against the refit direction); the default keeps the behaviour for all other users.
    
    MC truth (cosmic MC, 1073 muons crossing the inner region; true parameters at the bottom TPC inner radius propagated back through
    the closest approach to the top one, compared to the true momentum there, q16 / q50 / q84 in MeV): true loss between the two
    14.5 / 16.1 / 19.9 MeV (median for |z| at the closest approach 0-25 / 25-50 / 50-75 cm); predicted - true with the sign of the
    upward fit -14.5 / -15.2 / -18.6 MeV (as without material: the gain inward and the loss outward cancel), with the sign along the
    flight +1.2 / +2.1 / +1.0 MeV (spread q16-q84 about -2 ... +9 MeV). The matched cosmics hardly change because the two halves'
    errors cancel in their average: cosmic MC 7003 -> 7006 correct pairs (0 wrong), chi2Match median unchanged; cosmics run 562658
    358 cosmics before and after; refitted q/pt within +-0.05 %. The halves themselves (e.g. the momentum at the TPC entrance) change
    by the full loss.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * Cosmics: collect the raw clusters of matched cosmics and tag them with TOF (--enable-cluster-output)
    
    The async reconstruction stores neither TPC tracks nor TPC clusters, so the leg references of TrackCosmics cannot be resolved
    offline. New device cosmics-cluster-collector (+ cosmics-full-writer -> o2_cosmics_full.root, tree cosmicsFull, one entry per TF):
    - per cosmic (o2::dataformats::CosmicTrack, DataFormatsGlobalTracking): the TrackCosmics, the TPC tracks of both legs, the raw
      ClusterNative + sector/row of each leg's attached clusters and of all clusters in a road around the leg (flags: attached / road /
      used by any TPC track / found with the absolute time on the other TPC side), the ITS compact clusters (chip, anchor pixel, pattern
      ID, ROF BC; pattern bytes for patterns not in the dictionary), TOF clusters (raw time, ToT, channel), TRD tracklet words (+ trigger
      BC), MC label; per TF: TFIDInfo and vDrift / t0 of the TPC transformation. Only raw detector data are stored: TPC transformation,
      TOF calibration, ITS dictionary and geometry are applied offline.
    - TPC road: each leg's helix through all pad rows of its side, in the frame of its own time0, at the real x of the row, points beyond
      the leg's closest approach skipped; predicted real (y, z) mapped to nominal coordinates with the inverse correction; clusters within
      --corridor-width (1 cm) taken. The other TPC side is searched when the time of the cosmic is known (CE-crossing leg, z-continuity
      time with error < --max-abs-time-err 0.5 mus, or a TOF time).
    - TOF tag: all TOF clusters within the cosmic's time window and the road (--tof-road-width 5 cm) are candidates per leg; the top/bottom
      pair whose time difference matches the muon's flight along the helix (|t_top - t_bottom + L/c| < --tof-flight-tolerance 2 ns, z of
      one-side legs shifted to the pair's mean time) gets HitTOFFlight and the cosmic its TOF time (CosmicTrack::timeTOFMUS); without such a
      pair the closest hit per leg is kept. The same search in the impossible order (bottom hit first) only finds accidental pairs: its
      best score is stored next to the flagged pair's (scoreTOFPair / scoreTOFReversed) as QA of the flag's background.
    - The TOF time (--tof-time-error 0.1 mus) then fixes the other-side TPC corridor, the TRD road (trigger and z, --trd-road-width) and the
      ITS road (readout frame and z, --its-road-width); without it the TPC time is used.
    - Duplicates: per TF the cosmics are ranked (TOF time first, then more attached TPC clusters); one sharing >= 30 % of the smaller one's
      TPC clusters with a better one gets duplicateOf = that one's entry (a leg split into two TPC tracks). Nothing is removed.
    - Polish: cosmics with a TOF time are refitted at it (TPC-only legs: bottom leg inward to the closest approach to the beam line, top
      leg inward to the same point, halves combined; muon mass and energy loss along the flight as in the matcher), CosmicTrack::polished
      with chi2MatchPolished (< 0: not polished). The matcher's time is the bracket-overlap centre for one-side legs on the same side
      (tens of mus off), which puts the inner material at the wrong z. Check: polished at the matcher's time instead, the cosmic MC
      reproduces the matcher (chi2Match median 79.1 vs 79.2, q/pt within 7e-4).
    - Legs nearly parallel to the pad rows (closest approach to the beam line inside the TPC or at its inner edge): the row-by-row road
      cannot reach the rows, there the helix is followed in steps of path length and the rows within the road width are searched.
    - A TOF time can be negative (cosmic just before the TF start): the flag is CosmicTrack::hasTOFTime() (scoreTOFPair >= 0).
    - At most --max-cosmics-per-tf (100) cosmics per TF are written (protection against fake-dominated settings).
    - --debug-tree: cosmics_collector_debug.root, tree "cosmics" with one entry per cosmic (matching and timing quantities, vectors of the
      transformed TPC clusters, road points, ITS / TOF / TRD hits). Off by default.
    
    Validation: the road re-finds 99.8 % of the legs' own clusters in the cosmics run 562658 and 97 % in PbPb 2025 with the v10n correction
    map. PbPb 2025 LHC25an 567939 (600 TFs, preset physics-v1): 30 of 224 cosmics TOF-tagged (10 with legs on opposite TPC sides, 20 on one
    side), 0 pairs in the impossible order (flag purity >= 90 % at 95 % CL), flight-time residual centred at 0 within 0.2 ns; 10 duplicates.
    568041 reconstructed from CTF (10546 TFs): 3203 cosmics, 435 TOF-tagged non-duplicates, 90 duplicates. CPU: matcher + collector
    ~0.6 s per PbPb TF; output ~1.5 kB per TF.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * MatchCosmics: compare same-side TPC-only legs refitted at a common time
    
    A TPC-only track has no time measurement: its time0 is the tracker's guess
    (GPUTPCGMTrackParam::ShiftZ: z = 0 at the beam line if the helix can come
    from it, otherwise the latest cluster at z = 0.521 * x, then clamped to the
    drift volume). For a cosmic, which does not come from the beam line, the
    two legs get independent guesses, typically tens of mus apart, so their
    clusters were distortion-corrected at different z and the legs disagree
    (y, snp, q/pt) although they are one track. For legs on opposite sides the
    time comes from z continuity, but legs on the same side were compared as
    tracked.
    
    New MatchCosmicsParams refitSameSideAtCommonTime (default false, not in
    the preset physics-v1, see below): after the cheap cuts (tgl, q/pt, same half), same-side
    TPC-only legs are refitted at the centre of their brackets' overlap (the
    time the refit of the winners uses) and compared there
    (MatchCosmics::refitSeedAtTime: TPC refit from the outer parameters, then the
    propagation to the DCA as for the seeds; energy loss along the muon's flight
    as in refitWinners). The TPC refitter is created once per TF in process() and
    shared with refitWinners. The matcher debug tree writes the legs compared
    and a commonTime flag.
    
    Cosmic MC with PbPb-like distortions (190 TFs, preset physics-v1, off -> on):
    correctly matched muons 6848 -> 7324 of 8639 (79.3 -> 84.8 %); same side
    77.0 -> 84.2 %, its loss to the crude chi2 cut 6.9 -> 0.8 %; A×C unchanged;
    0 wrong-muon pairs in both; matcher +12 ms per TF (~100 refits). With the
    true MC time instead of the window centre the same-side pass rate of the
    chi2 cut would be 99.2 % (centre 98.0 %, legs at their own time0s 84.7 %).
    PbPb 2025 (4 TFs): ~530 refits per TF, +15 ms per TF.
    
    Not in the preset: in PbPb (568041, 310 CTFs, 16541 TFs) it adds mostly
    pairs of collision tracks, whose time0 was about right and which the
    refit at the window centre mis-corrects: +352 same-side cosmics but only
    +5 TOF-tagged (2.6 % of the new ones vs 15.3 % of the common ones), and
    ~35 A×C cosmics lose a leg to a refitted same-side pair.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * MatchCosmics: TOF flight pair of the legs as selection criterion
    
    New MatchCosmicsParams tofFlightSelection (default off, on in the preset
    physics-v1; needs TOF clusters, the workflow then adds them to the
    matcher's inputs): every pair of TPC-only legs accepted by checkPair is
    tested for a top / bottom TOF cluster pair along the outward
    continuations of its legs whose time difference matches the muon's
    flight between them along the helix (tofFlightTolerance), with the mean
    time in the pair's time window and both legs' y and z within tofRoad at
    that time (the test of the cluster collector). A confirmed pair takes
    the TOF time as its common time (error tofTimeError), so the winner is
    refitted at it, and is put in front of all unconfirmed partners of both
    legs (chi2 order within each group): the mutual-best selection prefers
    it, and a random pair can no longer take a leg of a TOF-confirmed cosmic.
    
    If the refit of a confirmed winner at the TOF time fails (in practice
    chi2Match > maxChi2Match), it is refitted at the time it has without its
    TOF flight pair (z-continuity time of legs on opposite sides, else the
    centre of the overlap of the legs' time brackets): the winner selection
    has already released the other candidates of both legs, so dropping the
    winner loses both legs. PbPb 568041: 24 TOF-tagged same-side cosmics,
    all real (legs on one line far from the beam line, TOF pair in the
    physical order without a reversed-order alternative), mostly on the C
    side nearer the readout at the TOF time; A-C cosmics show no TOF-TPC
    time offset there. The refit loop body is a lambda refitting a winner at
    a given time.
    
    The TOF candidates of a leg are searched once per TF, in the time-sorted
    TOF clusters of its time bracket and in the sector it points to and its
    neighbours. Debug tree "match": tofScore.
    
    Distorted cosmic MC (19 x 10 TFs, PbPb-like distortions, physics-v1
    without the common-time refit, without -> with tofFlightSelection):
    matched muons 6848 -> 6871 of 8639, 0 wrong pairs both, 2134 confirmed
    pairs, 9 fallbacks.
    
    PbPb 568041 reconstructed from CTF (310 CTFs, 16541 TFs, vs. the same
    CTFs without the TOF selection, older code, before the fallback):
    cosmics 4782 -> 4760, TOF-tagged 681 -> 697; A-C: 11 untagged pairings
    replaced by 12 TOF-tagged ones. Matcher CPU 0.536 -> 0.545 s per TF.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
