    * MatchCosmics: legs near the beam line for TOF-confirmed pairs only
    
    The seed cuts minSeedDCAxy / minSeedDCAxyNSigma (3 cm / 10 sigma in
    physics-v1) reject the legs of collision tracks, but also the cosmics
    crossing the ITS inner barrel (L0 / L1 entirely, L2 mostly). Loosening
    them floods the matcher with collision-track pairs (PbPb 567939, 600 TFs:
    1 cm / 3 sigma gives 38x more candidates, TOF-tagged 0.1 % vs 14 %).
    
    New MatchCosmicsParams minSeedDCAxyTOF (default -1: off) and
    minSeedDCAxyNSigmaTOF (3): with tofFlightSelection, TPC-only legs failing
    the seed DCA cuts but passing these looser ones are kept, flagged nearBeam,
    and used in TOF-confirmed pairs only: a pair with such a leg and no TOF
    flight pair is rejected (RejNoTOF) before it is registered, so it cannot
    compete in the winner selection or reach the cluster collector. Log line:
    seeds near the beam line and their confirmed pairs per TF.
    
    The cosmics carry TrackCosmics flags NearBeamBottom / NearBeamTop (new
    member, class version 2) for legs kept only by the looser cuts, so these
    cosmics can be selected or dropped downstream without redoing the seed
    cuts.
    
