    * CosmicsClusterCollector: ITS road keeps the 5 closest clusters per inner-barrel layer
    
    Near the beam line the road in the inner barrel is dense with collision
    clusters, and the TPC prediction there (~mm) does not single out the
    cosmic's hit: keeping only the closest cluster per half of the cosmic and
    layer often stores a random one. In layers 0-2 the 5 closest are now
    kept, best first (the first is the previous choice); the outer barrel
    keeps the closest. The insertion rejects a NaN score, as the single-hit
    comparison did. Only cosmics with |DCA_xy| < 3.8 cm cross the inner
    barrel, so the output grows only for those.
    
    PbPb 568041, 400 CTFs with near-beam legs (minSeedDCAxyTOF=0): first road
    hit of every (cosmic, half, layer) identical to the previous code, outer
    barrel unchanged, output +1.8 %. On near-beam tracks fitted in the outer
    barrel, 24 of the 31 inner-barrel hits on the track are not the closest
    road hit (the ranking is dominated by the z uncertainty).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
