    CcdbApi: Improved semaphore resource handling
    
    This commit improves on the semaphore handling in
    CcdbApi.
    
    Semaphore scopes/critical-sections using smart pointer approach
    - no explicit cleanup by user needed
    - code reduction
    
    Example:
    ```
    {
      std::unique_ptr<CCDBSemaphore>(snapshotpath, CCDBpath);
      // code in this scope is protected from running at the same
      // time in multiple processes
    
    }
    ```
    
    Moreover, a static registry class ensures
    that semaphores are "posted/removed" even if the critical
    section that the semaphore protects invokes signal handlers
    (SIGSEGV, ...). This works because static objects are usually destructed
    in any case.

