    Without this commit, one has to explicitely use ROOTSerialized, but it would not work to deserialize anyway:
    ```
    // on the sender side:
    ctx.outputs().snapshot({"out"}, ROOTSerialized<decltype(vec)>(vec));
    
    // then on the receiver side:
    auto dataRef = ctx.inputs().get("vector");
    auto vec = DataRefUtils::as<ROOTSerialized<std::vector<TObject*>>>(dataRef);
    
    // these fail during runtime
    // auto vec = ctx.inputs().get<std::vector<TObject*>>("vector");
    // auto wrapper = ctx.inputs().get<ROOTSerialized<std::vector<TObject*>>>("vector");
    ```
    With this commit, has_root_dictionary recognizes also pointers to objects with ROOT dictionaries in STL containers.
    Thus, the previous example becomes:
    ```
    // on the sender side
    ctx.outputs().snapshot({"out"}, vec);
    
    // on the receiver side
    auto vec = ctx.inputs().get<std::vector<TObject*>>("vector");
    ```

