    Option for PreHadron pruning in Pythia8 events
    
    Implementation of a pruning-filtering during Pythia8 event generation, with the effort
    to strip information before hadronization. The motivation is to considerably reduce
    the event-size and space taken in AOD or MC kinematics format.
    
    The filter removes all particles not satisfying the criterion of HepMC status
    code 1 or 2 (which essentially keeps particles from hadronization ... stable or not).
    Eventually some other filter criterion could be used (for instance based on Pythia8 status codes).
    
    The filter can be activated/deactivated using configurable parameter:
    
    GeneratorPythia8.includePartonEvent = [false|true] (default is false)
    
    A first quick test has shown that events are reduced by a factor of ~2 roughly.
    
    Relates to https://alice.its.cern.ch/jira/browse/O2-4257

