    - When EMCal gamma or jet triggers are used during data taking, these
      events have to be rejected as otherwise the energy spectrum would have
    turn-on curves, which might result in a wrong calibration of time and
    bad channels. Therefore, only specific triggers are allowed in the
    analysis.
    - The selection of triggers can be configures via the calib params. A
      string of : speparated trigger names can be defined there. Only those
    triggers will be selected.
    - The trigger names are checked at the initialization in finaliseCCDB
      (each time the CTP config changes) and mapped to the corresponding
    trigger bit
    - For each emcal trigger, the bc from the ctp is matched with the bc of
      the emcal event and it is then checked if one of the selected triggers is contained in
    the current event

