    [EMCAL-565, EMCAL-566] Update bad cell and time calibration
    
    - Several smaller things were improved using the apass2 offline
      recalibration
    - For low statistics runs, it can occur that more than half of the cells
      have 0 entries in a certain energy interval. The mean and sigma
    calculated in that case would be 0 as the truncation takes into accoutn
    only 50% of the data. If the mean and sigma are found to be smaller than
    0.0001, a refit is performed using 95% of the data for the truncation
    - The bad channel calibration uses the info of the cell time in order to
      cut on the width of the time distribution. Now, a certain window
    aroudn the peak of the time distribution is sonsidered instead of the
    full range, making the mean and sigma of the fit much more reliable.
    This was of special importance for the low IR runs where a single hit
    outside the main time peak would flag the cell as bad as it would differ
    to much from the other cells
    - For both changes, the getVarianceBoost1D and getMeanBoost1D was
      modified such that one can restrict it to a certain range

