    DPL: workaround fairmq::Socket::Receive behavior
    
    Receive will not actually be interrupted (as of FairMQ 1.4.56) when
    in Ready state and a State transition is requested. This will only
    happen once you get some message, with the net result that some
    early message might be cleaned up.
    
    With this change we periodically check for the state change ourself
    and we make sure that all the loop went over the state change at
    least once before moving to the next state. Whenever a state change
    is active, we also keep the messages and we do not merely drop them.
    
    This is not race condition free, but it should minimise the risk that
    certain messages get lost.

