    DPL: try keeping the average timer period duration as requested regardless jitter
    
    In case that uv_timer fires slightly before it should, `timerDrivenCreation` callback
    does not create a timeslice, thus delaying it until the next time, which is then later
    than anticipated. By incrementing the `last` instead of assigning it the `current`,
    we are able to recover to the requested period at least on average.
    
    If `last` is much behind, then we avoid performing many super-short cycles, as it may
    result e.g. in spamming QC mergers.

