    [O2-3142] DPL: fire uv_timer in smaller intervals
    
    This is an attempt to fix the issue of poor randomness of the cycle shifts of QC tasks on EPNs.
    
    It appears that the uv_timer itself is actually never shifted, only the *last variable in
    `timeDrivenCreation` callback is. Thus, the two timers are out of sync and in the end we
    generate the timer input only once the uv_timer fires. The problem did not appear with DPL driver,
    because the main loop was being triggered due to different reasons (e.g. WebSocket events), which
    do not take place when a data processor is executed on its own, like in ODC-controlled environment.
    
    This is a rather crude way to fix it by increasing the period of uv_timer by `resolution` and relying
    on the `timeDrivenCreation` callback to check if enough time elapsed. I confirmed that the CPU usage with
    a cycle of 10s stays below 1%, so the performance impact seems to be negligible. However, a nicer
    solution would be probably to control the timer from within the `timeDrivenCreation` callback and
    somehow detect when this timer has fired (but not the others).

