    MCH: properly configure the slot finalization (#10566)
    
    * [MCH] improve logic of slot finalization
    
    The check of the slot statistics and the slot finalization are explicitly
    done in the calibrator code instead of relying on the `checkSlotsToFinalize()`
    function, because for MCH we only have one slot that spans the whole run.
    
    `setUpdateAtTheEndOfRunOnly()` is also called at initialization to skip the
    internal check of the slot statistics at each TF.
    
    In the case where the calibrations are produced as soon as a target statistics
    is reached, the subsequent data is skipped to avoid producing multiple
    calibration objects for the same run.
    
    * [MCH] use mapping in pedestals calibration
    
    The electronics mapping is used to flag as valid the readout channels that
    are associated to detector pads. Only valid channels are processed and
    used to compute the total pedestals data size. Invalid channels therefore
    will not contribute to the computation when checking the statistics of
    a given calibration slot.
    
