    Optimization for AOD MC filling (part 1)
    
    This commit provides a considerable speed gain
    for MC-AOD conversion by speeding up the MC particle table filling.
    The overall speed improvement is ~45% for pp timeframes
    and ~75% for PbPb timeframes.
    
    This improvement is achieved via:
    
    a) restructuring of the data structure keeping track
       of which MC particles survive in AOD (mToStore):
    
       - use a simple hashmap per source and event instead
         of a hash map of combined source,event,track triples. The latter
         needs to much CPU time in hashing and access.
    
    b) do not loop over all particles uselessly (in some parts of the code):
       - we introduce a new (sorted) container keeping track of
         relevant particles over which we can loop which get's rid
         of some filtering
    
    Both measures contribute significantly to the gain.
    The changes have been validated using the MC release validation procedure
    on AODs.
    
    Note that the present optimization is step 1 in larger campaign:
    
    https://alice.its.cern.ch/jira/browse/O2-3240

