Author: Sandro Wenzel <sandro.wenzel@cern.ch>
Date:   Wed Sep 28 17:13:14 2022 +0200

    AOD: Optimization of search in bunch crossings (fillBCSlice)
    
    fillBCSlice was doing two binary searches in the std::map
    holding (sorted) bunch crossing timestamps.
    
    Since this function is called for many tracks T, the cost of
    fillBCSlice actually dominated the processing time for AOD creation in
    async reconstruction (O(T*log(N)), where N is the number of bunch
    crossings).
    
    Based on this observation, it makes sense to setup a dedicated lookup
    structure that makes searching in the bunch crossings faster.
    
    This commit provides such a structure, which follows the idea to bucketize
    bunch crossing times into cells (or time windows). In addition, cells know
    about their nearest filled neighbours for very fast navigation.
    So to get bunch crossing close to some time "t", one merely calculates an
    appropriate cell and just searches within the times located in that cell.

