    DPL: add Clang Thread Safety Analysis (#9628)
    
    By setting ENABLE_THREAD_SAFETY_ANALYSIS to ON, it enables
    support for the Clang / libC Thread Safety Analysis which
    allows to statically check thread safe behavior of code at
    compile time, with the help of some extra annotations.
    
    For the moment only an handful of framework classes are annotated
    but I suspect this could find general use in other parts of
    the code.
    
    The annotations can be included via "Framework/ThreadSafetyAnalysis.h"
    which sits in Framework/Foundation and therefore its actually
    usable everywhere, since it has no dependency on DPL and it can
    be used without linking the associated library.
    More information about Clang Thread Safety Analysis can be found
    at https://clang.llvm.org/docs/ThreadSafetyAnalysis.html.

