Author: Giulio Eulisse <10544+ktf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 24 10:33:48 2021 +0200

    DPL: handle race condition with many driver
    
    This seems to fix the race condition which was likely to
    happen with many readers. What was happening is:
    
    * Readers offered some memory, however, since we do not
      want to over-offer, we rely on metrics to know when the memory
      is really being consumed. This makes it such that initially
      some of the readers are offered less memory than what is actually
      needed to start.
    * A missing "flushBuffer" does not notify the driver that some memory
      is still available, so the memory is lost while we wait for it
      to be reported.
    * However, because we are idle, the monitoring metrics are not sent
      out, so the driver is never notified of the extra available memory,
      leading to an effective leak of resources.
    
    The main fix is to simply add a flushBuffer, so that the still available
    resources are notified and the driver can reschedule them.
    
    As a bonus, we tweak a bit parameters to reduce the period needed to stabilize
    the system.

