    This allows specifying a command to be executed after a given
    children has forked. For example it can be used to invoke numactl
    on the child pid and set it's numa parameters. A number of templated
    argument can be specified to customize the command based on the child process
    and parents properties. E.g.:
    
    {timeslice0} : the parallel processing timeslice (0 based index)
    {timeslice1} : the parallel processing timeslice (1 based index)
    {pid}: the pid of the child
    {id}: the id of the child
    {name}: the data processor name of the parent
    {rank0}: the rank of data parallel computation
    {maxRank0}: the max rank of the data parallel computation

