    Applying the DPL timeslice concept correctly for TPC digitizer workflow
    
    This is the final step to remove some workarounds from the early days of
    DPL. The first implementation of the TPC digitizer workflow has been using
    parallel processing of sector data by distributing the data over multiple
    time slices. While the TPC reco workflow has been changed already a while
    ago, this has been pending for the digitizer workflow.
    
    Sector data belonging together are now sent within one timeslice.
    This includes the following changes:
    - Using lane configuration of TPC reco workflow in digitizer workflow
    - Sending the context info for TPC sectors in one DPL timeslice (SimReader)
    - Defining custom dispatching policy set for the SimReader to publish immediately
      allows staggered processing of parallel data sets
    - setting completion policy for pipeline processors to process data as it
      comes in
    - Defining TPC part of digitizer workflow by using the DPL parallel-pipeline
      helper
    - Using one route per sector, the routes are distributed over the available
      processing lanes by the parallel-pipeline helper

