    Defining o2::itsmft::Cluster as messageable
    
    In order to safely detect messageable types they must be trivially copyable.
    It appears that o2::itsmft::Cluster is not trivially copyable, which is due
    to the underlying ROOT classes for Point3D.
    
    std::is_trivially_copyable<ROOT::Math::Cartesian3D> fails because the class
    implements a copy constructor, although it does not much more than the default copy
    constructor.
    
    A trivially copyable class is a class (defined with class, struct or union) that:
    
        uses the implicitly defined copy and move constructors, copy and move assignments,
        and destructor.
        has no virtual members.
        its base class and non-static data members (if any) are themselves also trivially
        copyable types.
    
    As one attempt, std::is_trivially_copyable has been specialized for Point3D, which is
    workign correctly. However adding Poin3D as a member still makes a simple struct
    non trivially copyable. Have to understand how the type trait is realized for class
    members.
    
    We believe that o2::itsmft::Cluster is messageable and explicitely specialize the
    type trait. A unit test is added to go beyond make-believe

