    TRD Digitizer Update O2-455 (#2069)
    
    * Improved digitizer performance
    
    More efficient way of passing the hits per detector at the cost of using some extra memory
    - Create an array of size 540
    - Each element of the array contains the hit collection for a given detector
    - Requieres only one loop per event over the full hit container
    - Previously we had Nevents * HitsContainerSize loops
    
    * Adding trd digits and digit index
    
    * Digit filling implemented
    
    - A map container is used instead of building look-up tables and prefilled signal vectors.
    
    * TRD digits produced
    
    - Digit type re-defined, it contains digit-index + adc array (fixed size @ 30 bins)
    - A map is used internally to avoid getting into the LUT used previously in AdcArray
    - The map allows to keep track only of the active pad for a given even (faster than loading all pad for lookup)
    - Many types are defined in Digit.h to keep changes flexible, especially with ADC_t
    - Full digitization chain working (hits to signals and signals to ADC)
    
    * digit container instead of digit in outputs
    
    * Dictionary for TRD digit
    
    - Needed for DPL ROOT serialization

