    * DCA minimizer for V0 finder [O2-712]
    
    DCA of 2 AliExternalTrackParam tracks, some documentation files on https://alice.its.cern.ch/jira/browse/O2-712
    
    Supports both DCA (unweighted) and Chi2 (weighted DCA) minimization. See testDCAFitter for example of usage
    
    Starts by finding analytical XY crossings (at most 2) and using them as seeds for non-linear minimization
    (the track errors used for Chi2 are evaluated only once at these seeding points).
    In case the PCA being fitted with one seed appears to be closer to alternative seed, the minimizaiton with
    this seed is abandoned. In some cases 2 seeds may produce 2 distinct PCA candidates,
    therefore one should check the DCAFitter::getNCandidates() result.
    
    See testDCAFitter.cxx for example of calls
    
    Files dcaMathFin.nb (dcaMathFinNoErr.nb) are Mathematica derivations of the chi2 (or DCA) 1st and 2nd
    derivatives used in the code for Newton-Rapson iterations.
    
    Todo:
    (1) At the moment the propogation is done the simple PropagateTo method using constant bz field.
        Need to inteface the fitter to o2::base::Propagator and consider material corrections.
    (2) More elaborate analysis of seeding XY points is needed, in most of cases with 2 crossings one
        of them can be rejected even w/o testing the DCA.
    
