    Fix desynchronizing of timer slot creation and timer expiration
    
    The timer mechanism had to timers - one for booking a new timeslot,
    another one for creating the message. After some time they would
    desynchronize, which caused situations, when a timeslot was created
    (by decision of creator callback), but the message itselft would not
    be created (because expirator being a **little** bit late).
    
    All of that resulted in having valid slots dedicated for timers, but
    they were never filled with a timer message. After some time, all of
    the slots were used by timers, and incoming data messages (with
    enumerated timeslices) was interpreted as obsolete.

