    Split compensator YOKE into outer shell and inner bulk
    
    This commit introduces the possibility to split the compensator YOKE
    into 2 parts: an outer shell where we can keep detailed physics and an inner
    part potentially useful for fast/cruder physics.
    
    The goals/reasonings are the following
    
    a) reduce CPU time caused by the YOKE (as indicated from measurements)
    
    b) mose secondaries that emerge are potentially from the skin of the material
       which motivates the split
    
    We can now systematically investigate how the skin thickness influences hit creation
    in other detectors and choose reasonable values.
    
    By default, nothing changes w.r.t. to the previous settings.

