      from the DPL processor function
      (any detector will typically have such a class which implements
       the actual transformation of hits to digits)
    
    - instances of digit and label containers
    
    - read the hits from the input chains
    
    - loop over all collisions and collision parts and pass
      in each case the hits to the digitizer
    
    Note that the logic in the DPL processor function is similar
    to the one in typical DigitizerTasks. The main difference is
    that we no longer use the FairRootManager to retrieve collisions times
    and input.
    
    Note that digits are not yet stored to file. This will be part of
    the next step: Forwarding hits to another component (such as one doing IO).
    
    The code here should be seen to describe the rough logic and how
    to reuse existing algorithmic components. It is expected that some stuff
    will be externalized into common service components (such as retrieval of hits, etc).

