    Adding the text-type storage for Huffman tables.
    
    Writing Huffman table to text file in self-constent format.
    One node definition per line. Each node has an index (corresponding to the
    line number). The tree nodes hold the indices of their child nodes.
    Leave node format: index value weight codelen code
    Tree node format:  index left_index right_index
    
        Example:
        0 value weight codelength code
        1 value weight codelength code
        ...
        n left right
    
    Reading from file:
    Either eof or blank line is explicitely required at the end of dump for
    reading. This correctly terminates the reading and leaves the rest of the
    file for subsequent model instance.
    The weight is added to the model while reading.

